  "question": {
    "text": "If pressure of real gas $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ in a container is given by $\\mathrm{P}=\\frac{\\mathrm{RT}}{2 \\mathrm{~V}-\\mathrm{b}}-\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{4 \\mathrm{~b}^{2}}$, then the mass of the gas in the container is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$32 \\mathrm{gm}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$16 \\mathrm{gm}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$4 \\mathrm{gm}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$64 \\mathrm{gm}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{P}=\\frac{\\mathrm{RT}}{2 \\mathrm{~V}-\\mathrm{b}}-\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{4 \\mathrm{~b}^{2}}$\r\n$\\left[\\mathrm{P}+\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{4 \\mathrm{~b}^{2}}\\right]=\\frac{\\mathrm{RT}}{2 \\mathrm{~V}-\\mathrm{b}}$\r\n$2\\left[\\mathrm{P}+\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{4 \\mathrm{~b}^{2}}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{V}-\\frac{\\mathrm{b}}{2}\\right]=\\mathrm{RT}$\r\n$\\left[\\mathrm{P}+\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{4 \\mathrm{~b}^{2}}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{V}-\\frac{\\mathrm{b}}{2}\\right]=\\frac{\\mathrm{RT}}{2}$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{n}=1 / 2 \\mathrm{~mole}$\r\n$\\therefore$ Mass of $\\mathrm{O}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 32=16 \\mathrm{gm}$"
  }
}